    "product_id": "6947efed-b5dd-40b7-8832-cf90625493bc",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 210722\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion \nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV \n1120 PM PST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* A few weak disturbances will roll through the area over the next \n  few days, bringing light snow showers to the Sierra and breezes \n  this afternoon and evening. Otherwise, weather across the rest of \n  the region will remain relatively benign with temperatures \n  trending warmer by next week.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\nUpper level trough that brought a few showers and gusty winds to \nsouthern Nevada this evening will continue to push east overnight. \nHigh pressure will then build over the region Saturday with lighter \nwinds and mostly sunny skies. Temperatures will remain rather cool \nSaturday with readings about 6 to 10 degrees below normal. We will \nremain in a rather progressive pattern for the next week with \noccasional troughs and ridges. The next trough is expected to pass \nthrough Sunday and Monday, but is expected to remain further north \nthan the previous system. This will bring snow chances for the \nSierra along with the shower chances for our northern zones, along \nwith increased afternoon breezes. This will be followed by another \nridge mid to late week with dry and mild conditions expected for \nThanksgiving. The next system looks to impact the area next weekend, \nbut again there is still plenty of spread in the models, but both \nthe deterministic GFS and EC are showing the potential of scattered \nshowers and gusty winds along with cooler temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package...\nWinds remain light around 8 kts becoming variable at times. Just \nafter 03z, winds are still on track to favor a more NNW direction \nand likely remain at 5-10 kts. SCT-FEW clouds at times over the \nterminal through the 09z timeframe. Precipitation is not expected to \nimpact the terminal, however there is a low (10-20%) chance of \nvicinity showers. If showers occur nearby, could see gusts around 20 \nkts. Guidance showing winds staying at a NNW direction through the \novernight hours until the early morning hours tomorrow then a more \nNNE direction around 17z, generally staying light around 6 kts. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCaliforniaFor the 00z Forecast Package\nQuiet weather conditions expected to continue through the TAF \nperiod. Few exceptions will be KDAG having strong winds today \naround 15 kts, 25 kt gusts, then becoming around 10 kts, 20 kt \ngusts this afternoon and persist into the evening hours and slowly\ndiminishing overnight. KVGT will have increasing winds this \nafternoon from the north just after 03z through 19z for KVGT \naround 10-12 kts. Guidance is showing precipitation in southern \nNevada but it is not expected to approach the terminal, however \nthere is a low (10-20%) chance of vicinity showers. If showers \noccur nearby, could see gusts around 20 kts. Expect light and \nvariable winds across all other terminals favoring from a \nnortherly direction. There is potential for strong northerly winds\nat KIFP during the early morning hours just after 17z with winds \nup to 10-12 kts. SCT-FEW clouds over most terminals this afternoon\nlasting till around the 8-12z time period and clearing out around\nthe 9-12z time period, with KEED and KIFP expected to have SKC \nconditions through the TAF period.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Gorelow\nAVIATION...Vinson\n\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
